      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Henrico lies adjacent to Lake Gaston, a 20,000‑acre reservoir on the Roanoke River formed by the Gaston Dam in 1963 for flood control, hydroelectric power, and recreation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/henrico_north_carolina",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The community maintains a rural character, with some development tied to lakeside tourism and historic sites in the Roanoke River watershed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/henrico_north_carolina",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The historic Dabbs House Museum in Henrico hosts a Tourist Information Center that opened in September 2010 and has welcomed almost 600 visitors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.naco.org/resources/award-programs/tourist-information-center",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Henrico’s early settlers were English, Scottish, Scotch‑Irish, and French Huguenot descendants who arrived from Virginia, drawn by the river’s navigability and fertile alluvial soils.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
